From eda434b9ea9eaf77e84f68710cb7aff94a25e40c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: testuser <mainta@example.test>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 04:19:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] fix(llms): send a Mantle model that cannot turn
 reasoning off its lowest advertised effort

An ACP session always runs with reasoning off (thinking false). On the Bedrock Mantle route that is
the portable reasoning "none", which @ai-sdk/openai writes as reasoning_effort "none". Mantle serves
the gpt-oss family (openai.gpt-oss-120b, -20b, gpt-oss-safeguard-120b, -20b) through Harmony, which
has effort levels and no off switch and answers HTTP 400 "Harmony does not support
reasoning_effort='none'". Measured 2026-10-03 against bedrock-mantle.us-east-1.api.aws (60 listed
models): those four return 200 with the field omitted or low and 400 with none; the 42 other models
that accept a plain chat request return 200 with none. The K3 row failed on those routes in 14 of 14
records.

resolveMantleReasoningFloor reads the model's reasoning controls from the catalog entry of its base
model id (the aws-mantle/ prefix and a geo-profile namespace removed) and returns the lowest
advertised effort when the model has effort levels and no off switch (no toggle, no "none"). The
Mantle params middleware replaces a reasoning "none" with that effort. A model with a toggle, with no
effort list, with an empty list or missing from the catalog keeps "none", an explicit effort is never
touched, and the Converse route is not involved. A provider-option reasoningEffort of none is
lowered the same way, because @ai-sdk/openai lets it win over the portable reasoning; the first catalog
entry that states reasoning options wins (a geo-profile entry without them falls back to the base entry);
a lowest advertised effort of max has no level the AI SDK can send and gives no floor.
